      "description": "Watch Inverness CT vs Partick highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 21, 2026. The Scottish Premiership took center stage on August 21, 2026 , as Celtic hosted Partick in a highly anticipated encounter. Fans filled the stands, eager to see how this early-season battle would unfold on the pitch. Early Dominance from the Hoops From the opening whistle, Celtic established their rhythm, dominating possession and forcing Partick into a defensive shell. The breakthrough arrived in the 26th minute when Benjamin Nygren found the back of the net with a clinical finish. The goal served as a catalyst for more pressure, as the home side looked to double their advantage quickly. That second goal arrived in the 38th minute, courtesy of Camilo Duran . The striker showed great composure to beat the goalkeeper, rewarding Celtic for their relentless attacking play. By the time the referee blew for half-time at 45+2' , the hosts held a comfortable lead and total control of the match momentum. Duran Doubles Up to Secure the Points The second half saw Partick attempt to stabilize, but Celtic remained sharp and clinical. In the 67th minute, the game was effectively put to bed. Benjamin Nygren turned provider, delivering a precise assist for Camilo Duran , who made no mistake in slotting home his second goal of the match to make it 3-0. A series of tactical changes followed, with Celtic introducing the likes of Reo Hatate , Anthony Ralston , and Liam Scales to see out the game. Despite a late yellow card for Kasper Joergensen in the 82nd minute, the hosts never looked troubled. The final whistle at 90+4' confirmed a dominant performance and a vital three points for the Glasgow giants."
